# project_requirements_document.mdc

## 1. Project Title
**E-Learn Portal** — Modular Video Education Platform

## 2. Purpose & Vision
The purpose of this project is to transform a previously embedded video education module from an e-commerce platform into a standalone, scalable learning management system (LMS) similar to Udemy. The system empowers organizations to create, assign, and track educational video content for employees, partners, or customers.

**Vision:** To create a centralized and user-friendly video-based learning environment with course structures, assignments, progress tracking, and interactive documentation support.

## 3. Target Users & Roles
- **Admin:** System owner with full access to user/role management, content, and system settings.
- **Team Lead:** Can create courses, manage team-specific content, assign content to users.
- **User:** Consumes assigned content, tracks progress, interacts with videos and documents.
- **Guest:** Limited access to preview content, encouraged to register for full access.

## 4. Core Features (Functional Scope)
- Authentication & Role-Based Access
- Video Management (YouTube-based)
- Course Creation & Management
- Video/Course Assignment to Users
- Video Watch Tracking & Progress Calculation
- Markdown-Based Document System (Notion-like)
- Notification System for Assignments
- Search & Filter by Category, Tag, Title
- Admin Panel for User, Role, Content Management

## 5. Functional Requirements
- Users must be able to sign up, log in, and manage their profile
- Admins can assign roles to users and revoke access
- Team Leads can create/edit courses and assign them
- Users can see only their own assigned courses and progress
- Videos must support metadata: title, duration, category, tags, YouTube URL
- Documents can be attached to courses or be standalone

## 6. Non-Functional Requirements
- The system must support responsive design (mobile/tablet/desktop)
- Must use secure authentication and RLS for database access
- System uptime: 99.5% availability for production deployment
- Dark mode must be supported
- Pages must load under 2s on average internet
- Localization-ready structure for future i18n support

## 7. Security & Privacy
- Supabase Auth for secure identity
- JWT session handling
- RLS enforced access rules
- Only Admins can view/edit all user data
- Guests have read-only access to public content

## 8. Success Criteria
- MVP delivered within 6 weeks
- Users can register, consume content, and complete assignments
- Admin can fully manage users and courses from panel
- Courses show real-time progress and completion
- Feedback and bug reports are addressable within 48 hours

## Summary
This PRD sets the foundation for the project's technical and business alignment. All derived features and implementation strategies must adhere to this vision unless justified via RFC. It serves as a north star reference for Cursor Agent, developers, and stakeholders. 